  "answer": "**Every new session restores on demand; no pre-started or pre-restored V2 instances were seen.** 20/20 new V2 sessions restored the version's snapshot (sessions shared 2 snapshot copies per runtime), each restored at most 0.09 s before its first request arrived (20/20 \u22642 s), and before the first session nothing was booted or restored outside the snapshot build. V1, for comparison, does keep a warm pool: 20/20 V1 sessions landed on their own instance that had been booted ahead of time (median 10.5 min before the session, newest 13 s), ran ~3.3 s, was frozen, and was resumed ~0.14 s before the first request; 10 and 10 V1 instances had booted before the first session was even sent. At this low, sequential load that pool made V1's cold invoke (p50 590 ms) faster than V2's (p50 1.93 s)."
