  "snapshot_scope": "endpoint+version",
  "answer": "**The snapshot is per endpoint and version, not just per version.** Each endpoint restores the version it points to, but an endpoint gets its own snapshot build (minutes) even when another endpoint already has that version: with DEFAULT, LIVE and test all on v1, DEFAULT restored snapshot d8119717 (built by create); LIVE restored snapshot 0095c5db (built by endpoint_create:LIVE); test restored snapshot 40c27ba9 (built by endpoint_create:test); after the runtime moved to v2, every endpoint restored the version it pointed at: DEFAULT \u2192 marker m2; LIVE \u2192 marker m1; test \u2192 marker m2; 5 of 5 endpoint creates/updates built a snapshot of their own (3.1 min, 3.1 min, 3.1 min, 3.1 min, 3.1 min); re-pointing LIVE at v2 once nothing referenced it restored a snapshot built by endpoint_update:LIVE; **the same runtime version ran different images on different endpoints**: test on the version with marker m1 ran B-r1027191511 (first seen with A-r1027191511). The version stores the image tag, and every snapshot build (a new endpoint, an endpoint update) resolves that tag again, so with a mutable tag re-pointing an endpoint at an old version does not bring back the old image."
 },
